      <workList xml:id="workDesc_343f4a67">
         <work xml:id="work_d1e223220">
            <identifier label="SchW" xml:id="identifier_6c7cf15a">A4:Coll.005</identifier>
            <title xml:id="title_53211cb3" xml:lang="fr">Pieces au clavessin </title>
            <title type="alternative" xml:id="title_c55d11e3" xml:lang="fr">VII pieçes pour le claveçin</title>
            <title type="alternative" xml:id="title_13a582f9" xml:lang="fr">VII pieces au clavecin</title>
            <contributor xml:id="respStmt_2d6f5cef">
               <persName role="composer" xml:id="persName_4e5e07fc">Johann Adolph Scheibe</persName>
            </contributor>
            <creation xml:id="creation_5c0aa2b5">
               <date isodate="1727" xml:id="date_a1e0f07f">1727</date>
               <geogName xml:id="geogName_1d665074">Leipzig,</geogName>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_1d2d8112">
               <p xml:id="idm128">The present collection of pieces or partitas for solo harpsichord was composed in 1727 while Scheibe was still living in Leipzig. Each partita consists of a number French dances. It is possible that Breitkopf acquired the work either from the estate of <persName xml:id="idm129" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">Carl Gotthelf Gerlach</persName>, cantor at Neukirche in Leipzig, or directly from Scheibe who sent manuscripts of works to Breitkopf – even when he had moved to Copenhagen (cf. SchW A4:001, A4:Coll.001, A4:Coll.004) – and for which he might have received a fee. Apparently Scheibe added another partita (SchW A4:106) to the collection before 1761, and all the works were hence placed in the same folder at Breitkopf (sometime during the nineteenth or early twentieth centuries, the insertion was removed and placed separately). The collection was advertised in the Breitkopf catalogue of 1761, and two years later in another catalogue, this time including incipits of all the first movements of the pieces or partitas. Finally the collection was auctioned in 1836 and bought by the collector <persName xml:id="idm130" auth="VIAF" auth.uri="http://www.viaf.org" role="">O.K.F. von Voß-Buch</persName>.</p>
            </history>
            <langUsage xml:id="langUsage_bd3341f6">
